# Christoph TPTP Benchmark on Helma

This notebook compares the six theorem provers requested for the TPTP benchmark:

- LEO-II
- Zipperposition
- E-Prover
- Vampire
- LEO-III
- ShotTx

The workflow is deliberately split into two phases:

1. Small smoke test to verify that Helma, the prover images, SLURM, and result collection all work.
2. Full TPTP benchmark only after the smoke test succeeds.

> Do not enable the full benchmark until the small test has been checked.

---

## 0. Install ATP Benchmark Runner

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:atp_benchmark_runner,
   github: "penthooose/atp_benchmark_runner",
   force: true}
])
```

---

## 1. Configure Livebook and Helma access

This opens the ATP benchmark setup form.

Enter the same Helma username and SSH key that you normally use.

```elixir
setup =
  AtpBenchmarkRunner.prepare_livebook_setup(
    submit_label: "Setup"
  )

env_map = setup.env_map
env_file = setup.env_file
ssh_key_path = setup.ssh_key_path

IO.puts("Setup completed.")
IO.puts("Cluster: #{env_map["HPC_CONNECT_CLUSTER"]}")
IO.puts("Username: #{env_map["HPC_CONNECT_USERNAME"]}")
IO.puts("TPTP root: #{env_map["TPTP_ROOT"]}")
```

---

## 2. Connect to Helma

```elixir
boot =
  HpcConnect.bootstrap(
    mode: :local,
    env_file: env_file,
    cluster: env_map["HPC_CONNECT_CLUSTER"] || "helma",
    username: env_map["HPC_CONNECT_USERNAME"],
    key_path: env_map["HPC_CONNECT_IDENTITY_FILE"]
  )

session = boot.session

IO.inspect(
  %{
    cluster: session.cluster.name,
    ssh_alias: session.ssh_alias,
    username: session.username,
    work_dir: session.work_dir,
    vault_dir: session.vault_dir
  },
  label: "Resolved HPC session"
)
```

---

## 3. Select Christoph's six provers

```elixir
selected_provers = [
  :leo2,
  :zipperposition,
  :eprover,
  :vampire,
  :leo3,
  :shot_tx
]

IO.puts("Selected provers:")

Enum.each(selected_provers, fn prover ->
  IO.puts("  - #{prover}")
end)
```

---

## 4. Check that all six provers exist in Paul's runner

```elixir
available_provers = AtpBenchmarkRunner.Provers.names()

IO.inspect(available_provers, label: "Provers available in ATP Benchmark Runner")

missing_provers =
  Enum.reject(selected_provers, fn prover ->
    prover in available_provers
  end)

if missing_provers == [] do
  IO.puts("✅ All six requested provers are available.")
else
  IO.puts("❌ Missing provers:")
  IO.inspect(missing_provers)
end
```

---

# PHASE A — SMALL TEST

Before running thousands of TPTP problems, test the complete system with five small problems.

---

## 5. Download five small TPTP problems

```elixir
smoke_problem_names = [
  "GRP002+0.p",
  "GRP003+0.p",
  "LAT001+0.p",
  "PUZ001+0.p",
  "REL001+0.p"
]

{downloaded_smoke, smoke_download_warnings} =
  AtpBenchmarkRunner.download_tptp_problems!(
    smoke_problem_names,
    force: false
  )

IO.puts("Downloaded #{length(downloaded_smoke)} smoke-test problems.")

Enum.each(downloaded_smoke, fn problem ->
  IO.puts(
    "✅ #{problem.name} | status=#{problem.expected_status} | rating=#{problem.rating}"
  )
end)

if smoke_download_warnings == [] do
  IO.puts("✅ No download warnings.")
else
  IO.puts("⚠️ Download warnings:")

  Enum.each(smoke_download_warnings, fn warning ->
    IO.inspect(warning)
  end)
end
```

---

## 6. Select the smoke-test problems

```elixir
smoke_problems =
  AtpBenchmarkRunner.select_problems(
    names: smoke_problem_names
  )

IO.puts("Selected #{length(smoke_problems)} problems.")

Enum.each(smoke_problems, fn problem ->
  IO.puts("  - #{problem.name}")
end)

IO.puts("")
IO.puts(
  "Expected prover/problem attempts: #{length(selected_provers) * length(smoke_problems)}"
)
```

For five problems and six provers, this should say:

`30`

---

## 7. Inspect the required Helma prover images

```elixir
prover_structs =
  Enum.map(
    selected_provers,
    &AtpBenchmarkRunner.Prover.builtin!/1
  )

image_plan =
  AtpBenchmarkRunner.image_build_plan(
    session,
    prover_structs
  )

IO.inspect(
  image_plan,
  label: "Remote image build plan",
  limit: :infinity
)
```

---

## 8. Prepare missing prover images

### SAFETY SWITCH

Leave this as `false` until the image plan above has been checked.

When ready, change:

`prepare_images_now? = false`

to:

`prepare_images_now? = true`

and run this cell.

```elixir
prepare_images_now? = false

image_build_result =
  if prepare_images_now? do
    IO.puts("Preparing prover images on Helma...")

    AtpBenchmarkRunner.build_prover_images!(
      session,
      prover_structs,
      install_scripts: false,
      force: false,
      build_on_login_node: false
    )
  else
    IO.puts("Image build NOT started.")
    IO.puts("Change prepare_images_now? to true only when ready.")
    :not_started
  end

IO.inspect(image_build_result, label: "Image preparation result")
```

---

## 9. Validate the prover images

Run this only after the required images exist.

### SAFETY SWITCH

```elixir
validate_images_now? = false

image_validation_result =
  if validate_images_now? do
    IO.puts("Smoke-validating the six prover images...")

    AtpBenchmarkRunner.smoke_validate_images!(
      session,
      prover_structs
    )
  else
    IO.puts("Image validation NOT started.")
    IO.puts("Change validate_images_now? to true when ready.")
    :not_started
  end

IO.inspect(
  image_validation_result,
  label: "Image validation result",
  limit: :infinity
)
```

---

## 10. Create the small Helma benchmark plan

This does not yet run the benchmark.

```elixir
smoke_plan =
  AtpBenchmarkRunner.bootstrap(
    session,
    selected_provers,
    smoke_problems,
    mode: :hpc,
    hpc_mode: :single_node,
    single_node_mode: :sequential,
    node_size: :half,
    timeout_seconds: 30,
    wait_for_completion: false,
    prepare_images: false,
    extended_debug: false
  )

IO.puts("✅ Smoke benchmark plan created.")
IO.puts("Run ID: #{smoke_plan.id}")
IO.puts("Provers: #{length(selected_provers)}")
IO.puts("Problems: #{length(smoke_problems)}")
IO.puts(
  "Attempts: #{length(selected_provers) * length(smoke_problems)}"
)

IO.inspect(
  smoke_plan.metadata[:hpc],
  label: "HPC configuration"
)
```

---

## 11. RUN the small benchmark

### SAFETY SWITCH

Do not change this to `true` until Steps 1–10 are confirmed.

```elixir
run_smoke_benchmark? = false

smoke_results =
  if run_smoke_benchmark? do
    IO.puts("Starting SMALL Helma benchmark...")
    IO.puts("Run ID: #{smoke_plan.id}")

    AtpBenchmarkRunner.run_benchmark(smoke_plan)
  else
    IO.puts("Small benchmark NOT started.")
    IO.puts("Change run_smoke_benchmark? to true when ready.")
    []
  end

IO.puts("Collected #{length(smoke_results)} results.")
```

A complete small run should eventually give approximately:

`30 results`

because:

`6 provers × 5 problems = 30`

---

## 12. Small-run results table

```elixir
if smoke_results == [] do
  IO.puts("No smoke-test results yet.")
else
  AtpBenchmarkRunner.results_table(
    smoke_results,
    memory: true
  )
end
```

---

## 13. Small-run report

```elixir
smoke_report =
  if smoke_results == [] do
    nil
  else
    AtpBenchmarkRunner.report(
      smoke_results,
      smoke_plan
    )
  end

if smoke_report do
  IO.puts("Run ID: #{smoke_report.run_id}")
  IO.puts("Generated: #{smoke_report.generated_at}")
  IO.puts("")

  AtpBenchmarkRunner.print_report_markdown(
    smoke_report
  )
else
  IO.puts("No report yet.")
end
```

---

## 14. Comparison by prover

```elixir
if smoke_report do
  IO.puts("| Prover | Total | Solved | Failed | Solve Rate |")
  IO.puts("|--------|------:|-------:|-------:|-----------:|")

  Enum.each(smoke_report.by_prover, fn prover_result ->
    IO.puts(
      "| #{prover_result.prover} | " <>
        "#{prover_result.total} | " <>
        "#{prover_result.solved} | " <>
        "#{prover_result.failed} | " <>
        "#{Float.round(prover_result.solve_rate * 100, 1)}% |"
    )
  end)
else
  IO.puts("Run the smoke benchmark first.")
end
```

---

## 15. Compare the provers problem by problem

```elixir
if smoke_report do
  AtpBenchmarkRunner.print_per_problem(
    smoke_report
  )
else
  IO.puts("No smoke report yet.")
end
```

---

## 16. Inspect errors or unusual results

```elixir
if smoke_results != [] do
  AtpBenchmarkRunner.print_interesting(
    smoke_results
  )
else
  IO.puts("No results yet.")
end
```

---

# PHASE B — FULL TPTP PREPARATION

Do not start this phase until all six provers work in Phase A.

Paul's runner can download and extract the official full TPTP archive.

---

## 17. Show the official TPTP archive information

```elixir
archives =
  AtpBenchmarkRunner.tptp_archives()

IO.inspect(
  archives,
  label: "Official TPTP archives",
  limit: :infinity
)

IO.puts("")
IO.puts("Local TPTP root:")
IO.puts(System.get_env("TPTP_ROOT") || "not configured")
```

---

## 18. Download and extract the official TPTP archive

### IMPORTANT SAFETY SWITCH

Keep this `false` until we have checked the smoke-test results.

```elixir
download_full_tptp? = false

full_archive_result =
  if download_full_tptp? do
    IO.puts("Downloading/extracting the official TPTP archive...")

    AtpBenchmarkRunner.ensure_tptp_archive()
  else
    IO.puts("Full TPTP download NOT started.")
    IO.puts("Change download_full_tptp? to true only when ready.")
    :not_started
  end

IO.inspect(
  full_archive_result,
  label: "Full TPTP archive result"
)
```

---

## 19. Inspect how many TPTP problems are available

This cell is safe. It does not submit a benchmark.

```elixir
all_tptp_problems =
  AtpBenchmarkRunner.load_tptp_problems()

IO.puts(
  "TPTP problems currently available: #{length(all_tptp_problems)}"
)

all_tptp_problems
|> Enum.take(20)
|> Enum.each(fn problem ->
  IO.puts("  - #{problem.name}")
end)
```

This number is extremely important.

We will inspect it before starting the real benchmark.

---

# PHASE C — FULL BENCHMARK

Do not run this until the smoke test and TPTP problem count have been reviewed.

---

## 20. Prepare the full benchmark problem set

```elixir
full_problems = all_tptp_problems

full_attempt_count =
  length(full_problems) *
    length(selected_provers)

IO.puts("Full TPTP problems: #{length(full_problems)}")
IO.puts("Provers: #{length(selected_provers)}")
IO.puts("Potential prover/problem attempts: #{full_attempt_count}")
```

---

## 21. Full benchmark configuration

This only creates the plan.

It does NOT start the benchmark.

We will review these settings before using them.

```elixir
full_plan =
  AtpBenchmarkRunner.bootstrap(
    session,
    selected_provers,
    full_problems,
    mode: :hpc,
    hpc_mode: :single_node,
    single_node_mode: :parallel,
    node_size: :half,
    max_parallel_jobs: 6,
    timeout_seconds: 30,
    wait_for_completion: false,
    prepare_images: false,
    extended_debug: false
  )

IO.puts("FULL benchmark plan prepared.")
IO.puts("Run ID: #{full_plan.id}")
IO.puts("Problems: #{length(full_problems)}")
IO.puts("Provers: #{length(selected_provers)}")
IO.puts("Attempts: #{full_attempt_count}")

IO.inspect(
  full_plan.metadata[:hpc],
  label: "Full HPC configuration"
)
```

---

## 22. START FULL TPTP BENCHMARK

### BIG SAFETY SWITCH

LEAVE THIS FALSE.

We will only change it after reviewing:

- all six prover images
- the smoke-test results
- the number of TPTP problems
- total number of prover/problem attempts
- Helma execution configuration

```elixir
START_FULL_BENCHMARK = false

full_results =
  if START_FULL_BENCHMARK do
    IO.puts("Starting FULL TPTP benchmark...")
    IO.puts("Run ID: #{full_plan.id}")
    IO.puts("Problems: #{length(full_problems)}")
    IO.puts("Provers: #{length(selected_provers)}")
    IO.puts("Attempts: #{full_attempt_count}")

    AtpBenchmarkRunner.run_benchmark(
      full_plan
    )
  else
    IO.puts("FULL BENCHMARK NOT STARTED.")
    IO.puts("")
    IO.puts("This is intentional.")
    IO.puts(
      "Do not change START_FULL_BENCHMARK until the configuration has been checked."
    )

    []
  end
```

---

## 23. Recover the latest Helma run if Livebook disconnects

Do NOT use this unless a benchmark was already submitted.

```elixir
recover_last_run? = false

recovered_results =
  if recover_last_run? do
    AtpBenchmarkRunner.collect_last_hpc_results!(
      session
    )
  else
    IO.puts("Recovery not requested.")
    []
  end

IO.puts(
  "Recovered #{length(recovered_results)} results."
)
```

---

## 24. Full benchmark results

```elixir
final_results =
  cond do
    full_results != [] ->
      full_results

    recovered_results != [] ->
      recovered_results

    true ->
      []
  end

if final_results == [] do
  IO.puts("No full benchmark results available yet.")
else
  AtpBenchmarkRunner.results_table(
    final_results,
    memory: true
  )
end
```

---

## 25. Full benchmark report

```elixir
full_report =
  if final_results == [] do
    nil
  else
    AtpBenchmarkRunner.report(
      final_results,
      full_plan
    )
  end

if full_report do
  AtpBenchmarkRunner.print_report_markdown(
    full_report
  )
else
  IO.puts("No full report available yet.")
end
```

---

## 26. Final prover scoreboard

```elixir
if full_report do
  IO.puts("| Prover | Total | Solved | Failed | Solve Rate |")
  IO.puts("|--------|------:|-------:|-------:|-----------:|")

  Enum.each(full_report.by_prover, fn prover_result ->
    IO.puts(
      "| #{prover_result.prover} | " <>
        "#{prover_result.total} | " <>
        "#{prover_result.solved} | " <>
        "#{prover_result.failed} | " <>
        "#{Float.round(prover_result.solve_rate * 100, 1)}% |"
    )
  end)
else
  IO.puts("No full benchmark report yet.")
end
```

---

## 27. Full per-problem comparison

```elixir
if full_report do
  AtpBenchmarkRunner.print_per_problem(
    full_report
  )
else
  IO.puts("No full benchmark report yet.")
end
```

---

## 28. Inspect interesting failures/timeouts

```elixir
if final_results != [] do
  AtpBenchmarkRunner.print_interesting(
    final_results
  )
else
  IO.puts("No full benchmark results yet.")
end
```

---

## 29. Visual benchmark summary

```elixir
if final_results != [] do
  case AtpBenchmarkRunner.visualize(final_results) do
    :ok ->
      :ok

    markdowns ->
      Enum.each(markdowns, &IO.puts/1)
  end
else
  IO.puts("No full benchmark results to visualize.")
end
```

---

## 30. Cleanup temporary SSH key

Only use this when everything is finished.

```elixir
cleanup_now? = false

if cleanup_now? do
  AtpBenchmarkRunner.cleanup_livebook_setup()
else
  IO.puts("Cleanup skipped.")
end
```
